s=s.replace('The solid white car is your physical vehicle. The mint silhouette is a ghost projected onto the floor. An overhead virtual camera follows the roof marker.','The Red Bull-styled car is your physical vehicle. The cyan silhouette is a floor projection of the same detailed model. It follows Max Verstappen’s recorded qualifying lap; an overhead virtual camera follows your ArUco marker.')
s=s.replace('This is a browser simulation of a projection installation. The ghost is synthetic, the marker and camera tracking are visual simulations, and speed is scaled to full-size race-car units.','This is a browser simulation. The ghost uses historical OpenF1 telemetry. The circuit ribbon is reconstructed from that recorded line; width and limits are illustrative. ArUco detection is simulated. Vehicles are enlarged for tabletop visibility, and driving uses adjustable arcade physics.')
s=s.replace('</main><script type="module" src="app.js"></script>','''<dialog id="sources"><button id="closeSources" class="icon" aria-label="Close credits">×</button><div class="eyebrow">PROVENANCE / LOCAL DATA</div><h2>Real laps. Honest limits.</h2><p>Max Verstappen’s fastest available recorded qualifying lap at each circuit: Monza, Silverstone and Monaco, 2024. Historical data is downloaded locally from <a href="https://openf1.org/docs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenF1</a>. Playback preserves the recorded lap duration, varying speed, gear, throttle and brake values. Positions are interpolated between samples and a small timing-line closure correction prevents loop jumps.</p><p><a id="lapSource" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lap timing source</a> · <a id="positionSource" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Position source</a> · <a id="carDataSource" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Car telemetry source</a></p><p>The projected road follows the driver trace. Its width, kerbs and track limits are illustrative, not surveyed circuit boundaries. No claim is made that this is a mathematically optimal racing line.</p><p><b>Car:</b> <a href="https://sketchfab.com/3d-models/f1-2026-concept-polygon-model-ea3bde709b1e4dc9b0ec8557d106ed42" target="_blank" rel="noopener">F1 2026 concept by Qvist_designs</a>, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">CC BY 4.0</a>. The <a href="models/ATTRIBUTION.md">prepared mesh</a> is scaled, recolored navy/red/yellow, given Red Bull/Oracle text and an ArUco marker, and flattened for the ghost projection. This is a Red Bull-inspired livery on a concept chassis, not an exact RB20 model or an endorsed product.</p><p>Steering uses arcade handling with a short virtual wheelbase for tight corners. Camera tracking is a geometric simulation, not live OpenCV detection.</p></dialog><div id="loading"><strong>Preparing the grid</strong><span>Loading recorded telemetry and the detailed F1 model…</span></div></main><script type="module">import('./app.js').catch(error=>{console.error(error);const el=document.getElementById('loading');el.hidden=false;el.querySelector('strong').textContent='Unable to load simulator';el.querySelector('span').textContent=error.message+' · Reload to try again.'});</script>''')
p.write_text(s)
p=Path(__file__).parent/"dist"/"app.js"
